<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE hi2txt SYSTEM "hi2txt.dtd">
<hi2txt>
  <!--
    Centipede (Atari, 1980)

    Centipede's 8-entry table is split across two files by design:
      - earom : ranks 1-3, saved natively by the game's EAROM
      - .hi   : ranks 4-8, saved by the stock hiscore.dat hiscore plugin
    The stock hiscore.dat entry is:
        centiped: @:maincpu,program,000b,0f,10,01
                  @:maincpu,program,0023,0f,04,12

    RECOMMENDED SETUP (stock hiscore.dat):
    Run hi2txt against BOTH files. The two structures below are rank-aligned so
    their outputs dovetail into one correct 1-8 table with no merge step:
        earom structure -> RANK 1-3
        .hi (30-byte)   -> RANK 4-8 (loop start="3")
    The game keeps its table sorted and always routes the top 3 to the EAROM and
    ranks 4-8 to the .hi, so earom #3 >= .hi #4 always holds; the file boundary
    is exactly the rank 3/4 boundary, so the offsets can never mis-order.

    Do NOT extend hiscore.dat to dump all 8 into the .hi: its start marker would
    then sit on the volatile rank-1 score byte, and once the #1 default (16543)
    is beaten the EAROM restore changes that byte on boot, breaking the plugin's
    marker match. Leave the top 3 to the EAROM.

    The 48-byte .hi structure below is retained only to still read a full-dump
    file produced by that (discouraged) extended entry; it is not needed for the
    recommended stock setup.
  //-->

  <!-- full-dump .hi from the (discouraged) extended hiscore.dat: 48 bytes = all 8 -->
  <structure file=".hi">
    <check><size>48</size></check>
    <loop count="8">
      <elt size="3" type="int"  id="SCORE" endianness="little_endian" base="16"/>
    </loop>
    <loop count="8">
      <elt size="3" type="text" id="NAME"  charset="centiped" ascii-offset="64"/>
    </loop>
  </structure>

  <!-- RECOMMENDED: stock hiscore.dat .hi = 30 bytes, ranks 4-8 (RANK 4-8) -->
  <structure file=".hi">
    <check><size>30</size></check>
    <loop count="5" start="3">
      <elt size="3" type="int"  id="SCORE" endianness="little_endian" base="16"/>
    </loop>
    <loop count="5" start="3">
      <elt size="3" type="text" id="NAME"  charset="centiped" ascii-offset="64"/>
    </loop>
  </structure>

  <!-- RECOMMENDED: native EAROM = top 3, ranks 1-3 (RANK 1-3) -->
  <structure file="earom">
    <check><size>64</size></check>
    <loop count="3">
      <elt size="3" type="int"  id="SCORE" endianness="little_endian" base="16"/>
    </loop>
    <loop count="3">
      <elt size="3" type="text" id="NAME"  charset="centiped" ascii-offset="64"/>
    </loop>
  </structure>

  <output>
    <table id="HIGH SCORES" line-ignore="SCORE:0">
      <column id="RANK" src="index" format="+1"/>
      <column id="SCORE"/>
      <column id="NAME"/>
    </table>
  </output>

  <charset id="centiped">
    <char src="0x00" dst=" "/>
  </charset>
</hi2txt>
